<rml>
<head>
	<!-- Locale flag strip at the top of the login screen: replaces the legacy
	     strip (uilocaleselector.py) while the locale-strip flag is on
	     (controller: assets/root/nui_locale_strip.py). One flag per locale,
	     its native name as a hint; the flag of the locale in use is
	     selected. Nothing in it takes the focus, so a login field keeps its
	     caret; RmlUi then sends no click, so the flags act on mousedown. A
	     flag is a button, so a press plays the legacy click sound (G11's
	     mousedown rule for a button that takes no focus). -->
	<title>locale-strip</title>
	<link type="text/template" href="../../nui.rtpl"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="locale-strip.rcss"/>
</head>
<body template="nui" class="locale-strip" data-model="locale_strip">
	<button class="locale-strip__flag nui-has-tooltip" data-for="flag : flags" data-attr-id="'locale-flag-' + flag.code" data-class-is-selected="flag.code == current" data-event-mousedown="pick(flag.code, ev.button)"><img class="locale-strip__image" data-attr-src="flag.image"/><span class="nui-tooltip nui-anim">{{ flag.name }}</span></button>
</body>
</rml>
